## Section identity derivation

Section idents are PATH-DERIVED — composed from the parent memorial's ident plus the heading-chain slug:

```
memory/decisions/foo.md
├── ## Context              → :memory.decisions/foo__context
├── ## Decision             → :memory.decisions/foo__decision
│   ├── ### Alternatives    → :memory.decisions/foo__decision__alternatives
│   └── ### Acceptance      → :memory.decisions/foo__decision__acceptance
└── ## See also             → :memory.decisions/foo__see-also
```

When two headings would produce the same slug, the codec auto-disambiguates with `-2` / `-3` suffix.

## Sibling chain navigation

Sections form a doubly-linked chain via `:mm.section/next-sibling` + `:mm.section/previous-sibling` — pairwise (each pair declares both directions), allowing O(1) walk in either direction.  Per the SIOC sibling-chain pattern from the section-schema ADR.

## Composition with other classes

- **`:mm/Memory`** — memorial's `:mm.memory/first-section` entry-point begins the section chain
- **`:mm/Link`** — markdown links extracted from section body content reference back to the containing section via `:mm.link/in-section`

